    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "You're scared of debt. I love it. Let me show you why.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 2.73,
        "window": 3.4,
        "fill": 0.803
      },
      {
        "scene": "promise",
        "text": "Same bank, two loans. Rohan borrows $40,000, I borrow $100,000, and one question decides who gets richer.",
        "start": 3.7,
        "seconds": 8.05,
        "window": 8.7,
        "fill": 0.925
      },
      {
        "scene": "carbuy",
        "text": "Mine buys a shiny new car! Just 7% a year, paid over 60 months. Easy.",
        "start": 12.4,
        "seconds": 4.87,
        "window": 5.23,
        "fill": 0.931
      },
      {
        "scene": "carcost",
        "text": "But a car loses value every year you drive it. So Rohan pays $7,523 in interest for something that keeps shrinking.",
        "start": 17.63,
        "seconds": 8.06,
        "window": 8.73,
        "fill": 0.923
      },
      {
        "scene": "myloan",
        "text": "My loan costs 6% a year. Over 10 years, that's $33,225 in interest, even more than Rohan pays.",
        "start": 26.37,
        "seconds": 8.31,
        "window": 9.0,
        "fill": 0.923
      },
      {
        "scene": "buys",
        "text": "The difference is what I buy with it: a building, or a business that can grow.",
        "start": 35.37,
        "seconds": 3.69,
        "window": 4.33,
        "fill": 0.852
      },
      {
        "scene": "gains",
        "text": "If it grows an assumed 8% a year, in 10 years it gains $115,892.",
        "start": 39.7,
        "seconds": 6.6,
        "window": 7.27,
        "fill": 0.908
      },
      {
        "scene": "doubt",
        "text": "Hold on. You still pay the bank all that interest!",
        "start": 46.97,
        "seconds": 2.28,
        "window": 2.77,
        "fill": 0.823
      },
      {
        "scene": "turn",
        "text": "Gladly. The interest is my cost, the growth is my profit. Good debt buys something that earns more than the loan costs.",
        "start": 49.73,
        "seconds": 6.09,
        "window": 6.77,
        "fill": 0.9
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "That's why the rich love debt: the car shrinks, the building grows. But if what they buy stops growing, the loan still has to be paid.",
        "start": 56.5,
        "seconds": 7.34,
        "window": 8.0,
        "fill": 0.917
      },
      {
        "scene": "loop",
        "text": "So I'm not scared of debt. I'm scared of my car loan. And honestly, Sharma...",
        "start": 64.5,
